::CW_U05_L02_GP_Q01::[MLA.CW.REV.02] Draft sentence: Mara handed Lena the box after she dropped it, and it made her upset. Which revision is clearest?{
=A. After Maya opened the box, she handed the old photograph to Lena.#Correct. This revision names the people and object clearly so the reader knows who did what.
~B. She handed it over after it happened and it was upsetting.#Incorrect. This keeps the pronoun confusion. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
~C. The box was there and it was a thing.#Incorrect. This is vague. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
~D. They did it and then it happened.#Incorrect. This is even less clear. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
}

::CW_U05_L02_GP_Q02::[MLA.CW.REV.02] Draft: The rain stopped. I found the letter. The house was quiet. Which revision improves cohesion?{
~A. The rain stopped. I found the letter. The house was quiet.#Incorrect. This repeats the choppy original. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
~B. Letter quiet rain house found.#Incorrect. This removes sentence clarity. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
~C. I found quiet because rain letter.#Incorrect. This is not coherent. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
=D. When the rain stopped, I found the letter on the quiet porch.#Correct. This combines the ideas smoothly and shows the relationship between events.
}

::CW_U05_L02_GP_Q03::[MLA.CW.REV.02] Draft: i opened the door it was snowing Which revision fixes conventions?{
~A. i opened the door it was snowing.#Incorrect. Capitalization and sentence boundary issues remain. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
=B. I opened the door. It was snowing.#Correct. This uses capitalization and sentence boundaries correctly.
~C. I opened the door it was snowing.for this item#Incorrect. This still needs sentence separation or punctuation.
~D. opened door snowing i it was.#Incorrect. This is not standard word order. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
}

::CW_U05_L02_GP_Q04::[MLA.CW.REV.02] Draft: Jordan told Sam that he should leave because he was angry. What is the clarity problem?{
~A. The sentence has no characters.#Incorrect. Jordan and Sam are characters. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
~B. The sentence has too many commas.#Incorrect. There are no commas. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
=C. The pronoun "it" is unclear because readers do not know what Jordan gave Sam.#Correct. This identifies the clarity problem in the sentence.
~D. The sentence is already perfectly clear.#Incorrect. The pronoun reference is unclear. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
}

::CW_U05_L02_GP_Q05::[MLA.CW.REV.02] Which revision order is most effective for a creative draft?{
=A. Check meaning and structure first, then polish conventions.#Correct. Larger revision decisions should come before final editing.
~B. Fix conventions first, then ignore meaning.#Incorrect. Meaning and structure should not be ignored.
~C. Add random punctuation before reading the draft.#Incorrect. That does not support revision. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
~D. Remove every creative choice.#Incorrect. Revision should preserve purposeful voice. This choice is not supported by the provided context or lesson skill; choose the option grounded in the prompt.
}
